From 1991c801c55182d52bce256097eee503c3121828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viswesh Narayanan <viswesh.narayanan@broadcom.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:37:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] NIST curves hybrid KEX implementation

This implementation is based on the RedHat patch (patch 0047),
with the only deviation being that we allow mlkem768x25519-sha256
in FIPS mode (hybrids are OK if the classical key is non-FIPS
based on NIST SP 800-56C Rev 2).

Key Changes:

* Adds NIST Hybrid KEX: Introduces mlkem768nistp256-sha256 and
  mlkem1024nistp384-sha384 alongside the existing X25519 hybrid.

* FIPS Integration: Integrates all three methods with FIPS-tiering
  using OpenSSL's EVP API, properly gating availability based on
  what the OpenSSL FIPS provider supports. Note X25519 is used
  from upstream OpenSSH implementation.

* Code Refactoring & Bug Fixes: Consolidates KEX gating logic to
  prevent divergence, fixes error handling (e.g., properly reporting
  SSH_ERR_LIBCRYPTO_ERROR instead of silent failures), and ensures
  safe memory cleanup for hybrid client keys.

* File Restructuring: Splits the implementation into three files
  (kexmlkemevp.c, kexmlkemnist.c, kexmlkem768x25519.c) to cleanly
  separate OpenSSL helpers, NIST-curve hybrids,
  and the upstream X25519 code for easier future merges.
